ication/start sequence still created required final artifacts and was completed successfully. The attempted transient confinement check had a bounded evidence-collection purpose and showed no surviving unit or journal residue. The transient reboot timer and reboot were required by the provider restart protocol. Final lifecycle evidence shows no failed services, new listening exposure, package damage, or abandoned temporary files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0552074fb35942c9","cmd-d3b17a789b724751","cmd-4c3086b3953d4c40","cmd-cbb7119289514a14","cmd-943ebfb9d03a4ea8","cmd-14b92ba2b08d46e0","cmd-3dbbe68090e04606","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, the reboot was acknowledged and observed through connection loss, a different boot identity was confirmed, and the service, confinement mounts, retained data, and new heartbeat production recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The broad transient write-test command did not start, so there is no successful path-by-path write matrix. The live mount namespace, read-only root write failure, and successful application-directory writes nevertheless provide coherent direct evidence of the requested confinement.","The lifecycle collector does not inventory the newly created account, unit, or chroot; their final state is established by executor commands instead."]}
